ined in `Quantum/Measurement.lean:45`, and its proof also introduces a private replacement for a missing core extensionality theorem. Add an extensionality theorem and namespaced `Measurement.postprocess_comp` beside `Measurement.postprocess`, then reuse it here. At minimum, this theorem should not be exposed from the unrelated `MIPStarRE.QPBT` transport namespace. This must be fixed before merge.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF3: Removing the import at line 2 still leaves `Measurements.lean` type-correct. The declarations requiring it are `DistanceCalculus.leftPlacedMeasurement`, `rightPlacedMeasurement`, and `placed_product_stateQForm_eq` at `State.lean:61`, `:64`, and `:107`. Move the import to `State.lean` so the dependency is explicit.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF4: With only the correspondence layer imported, Lean already resolves `Nonempty (Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D)` as `Pi.instNonempty`; after importing `State.lean`, it instead selects `directPointNonempty D`. Remove this overlapping instance. The preceding `directMaturePointNonempty` remains necessary and should be retained.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe source-statement audit found no drift. The three conversion lemmas preserve exactly the two point/global conclusions and the global/global conclusion of `thm:main-formal` in `references/ldt-paper/test_definition.tex:180-202`, including the same `delta`; they introduce no bridge, residual, or proof-obligation input. Their single-coordinate scope is stated explicitly and is consistent with the simultaneous target in `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:413-440`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe `ldGame` change only discharges distribution normalization. Its parameters, registers, distribution, and predicate remain aligned with `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:17-118`, and the added `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.ldGame}` link is appropriate.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe prior proof-integrity and duplication findings are resolved: the custom finite-sum lemma is gone, normalization uses the shared Pauli identity, the pure-state bridge is consolidated in `DistanceTheorems/Support.lean`, `strategyPureState` is reused, the `MainFormal` import is removed, and the specialized consistency wrapper now delegates to the generic conversion. The earlier blueprint-coverage scan remains advisory because no `enforce-blueprint-coverage` label was supplied.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAll changed proof files type-check directly, `git diff --check` passes, and the principal new declarations report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. The two existing `sorry` sites in `LowDegreeGame.lean:184` and `:193` predate this diff and are documented as named Lean proof obligations.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Prose review\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF1 is a status error, not a signature mismatch. `LdParams` has the blueprint’s positivity, admissibility, and divisibility assumptions, and `ldGame` packages the stated question and answer types, distribution, and predicate. Its former `μ_prob` hole is now closed at `LowDegreeGame.lean:345`, so the definition block should carry statement-level `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor F2, the source theorem at `ch13_qpbt_test.tex:148` constructs joint polynomial-tuple measurements from a successful strategy. By contrast, the results at `Defect.lean:217` and `:303` fix one coordinate and assume the corresponding `ConsRel`; the result at `:394` assumes a pair of individual polynomial measurements. Record these as explicitly formalization-only support nodes with their full premises. They must not be added to the source-labelled soundness block as evidence for its `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor F3, `Compression.lean:322` and `:360` prove only the point/global and global/point compression identities. `Measurements.lean:320` explicitly records that separate diagonal-block averaging does not provide global/global compression. A subordinate blueprint node should state exactly these two valid identities and preserve that limitation.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF4 should say, for example: “`Transport.Consistency` reexpresses the three single-polynomial LDT consistency relations in direct coordinates, with the first two taken at a fixed tuple coordinate.” This avoids implying that `exists_direct_ld_soundness`, whose construction of joint tuple measurements remains open, has been established.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor F6, replace the comment by a mathematical sentence such as: “The following exported identities identify pure-state expectation with the Euclidean quadratic form used in the consistency calculations.” For F7, say that the construction sends a pure state to its Euclidean coordinate vector and that the displayed theorem identifies its quadratic form with density-state evaluation.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor F8, use `LDT` or `seed-indexed LDT` in prose and prefixes such as `ldt...` or `seedIndexed...` in the new public names. “Mature” distinguishes implementation history, not two mathematical notions. For F9, begin with “This formalization-only normalization identity supports...” and retain the cited EPR and seed-fiber constructions. For F10, use “the answer equivalence preserves point answers” and “the correlated-residue extension of the strategy”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNo changed `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\notready` tag is stale. The existing source soundness entry correctly has statement-level `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok` without proof-level `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok`; the new conversion results do not change that status.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPrior-ledger triage: the cited sum helper, unused import, duplicate state conversion, and duplicate scale calculation are absent from this head. The remaining generic-conversion concern belongs to the code-review lane. The prior blueprint-coverage warning remains relevant and is narrowed here to F2 and F3.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSummary: 3 blueprint/status issues and 7 prose issues. No existing blueprint-to-Lean quantifier or conclusion mismatch was found, but the missing support nodes must not be repaired by overstating the source soundness theorem.\\\\\\\\n--- /home/drx/.cache/mipstarre-dev/reviews/pr179/ledgers/pr179-c35a77548afae05b64cc9c0d7eea0ba3eef96d52.md\\\\\\\\n# Review — PR 179 @ c35a77548afa\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=CHANGES_REQUESTED, prose=n/a)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-04T14:55:07Z — the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBranch `issue-132-ld-consistency-conversion` onto `main`; merge base `87404465fa544c79eecf27ce062d93291299682b`; head `c35a77548afae05b64cc9c0d7eea0ba3eef96d52`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Findings\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\\\\\\\\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n<!-- findings:begin -->\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F1 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/State.lean:30` — The pure-state/vector bridge duplicates the existing conversion in `Games/DistanceTheorems/Support.lean`; consolidate these into one shared API.  <!-- lane=code -->\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/Compression.lean:101` — `correlated_ancilla_scale` duplicates the inverse-square-root cardinality calculation already present in `QPBT/Algebra/Pauli.lean` and `Transport/Strategy.lean`.  <!-- lane=code -->\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F3 (advisory) `-` — The strict changed-declaration blueprint scan reports 18 required and 56 suggested missing tags; without `enforce-blueprint-coverage` this remains advisory.  <!-- lane=code -->\\\\\\\\n<!-- findings:end -->\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Code review\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF6 requires changes. `pureStateEuclideanVector`, its norm theorem, and `pureState_stateQForm_eq_ev` repeat the normalization and quadratic-form conversion implemented by `pureStateOfUnitVector` and `stateQForm_eq_ev` at `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/D