e 188. The current `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok` must not remain on the broader statement.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF2 was not resolved by renaming the earlier `mature...` declaration. Its proof is exactly an application of `strategyConsRel_consistencyDefect_le`, and its only substantive consumer is the immediately following direct-coordinate theorem; the reverse direction already invokes the generic result directly. Inline that application and update the stacked branch rather than retaining a duplicate public specialization and compatibility alias.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe other prior findings are addressed: the Mathlib-duplicate sum lemma is gone, generic consistency and measurement lemmas are correctly placed, imports are direct, normalization is shared, and the blueprint now records the restricted coordinate and compression results. The facade type-check and `git diff --check` both pass. The authoritative patch introduces no `sorry`, axiom, or kernel bypass; its sole `sorry` match is the removed `ldGame.μ_prob` proof hole. Existing imported proof holes remain explicitly documented as named obligations.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Prose review\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF1 is a substantive equivalence mismatch. The blueprint imposes `δ ≥ 0`, globally assumes a projective strategy, and calls `Gᴬ,Gᴮ` merely “measurements” at [ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1945](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-132-ld-consistency-conversion/blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1945). The first two Lean declarations quantify over every real `delta` and require both `S.IsProjective` and projective polynomial measurements at [Defect.lean:106](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-132-ld-consistency-conversion/MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/Defect.lean:106) and [Defect.lean:192](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-132-ld-consistency-conversion/MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/Defect.lean:192). The third declaration does not require `S.IsProjective` at [Defect.lean:283](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-132-ld-consistency-conversion/MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/Defect.lean:283). State `δ ∈ ℝ`, call the polynomial measurements projective, and restrict projectivity of the strategy to the first two items, potentially by splitting the entry.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF2 is the explicit indexing mismatch: [ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1949](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-132-ld-consistency-conversion/blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1949) uses `r ∈ {1,…,k}`, while the Lean declarations use `r : Fin D.k`, hence `r ∈ {0,…,k-1}`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF3 invalidates the compression block’s statement-level status. The linked declarations at [Compression.lean:322](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-132-ld-consistency-conversion/MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/Compression.lean:322) and [Compression.lean:360](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-132-ld-consistency-conversion/MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/Compression.lean:360) prove the two mixed compression identities only. They do not formalize the assertion that the two global/global quantities do not bound one another. Move [the negative assertion](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-132-ld-consistency-conversion/blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:2008) into a separate remark without `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor F4 and F5, both new lemma blocks end without proof environments. All five linked Lean theorems are completed; their axiom reports contain only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. After correcting F1-F3, add concise `proof` environments carrying proof-level `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor F6, replace “mature low individual degree test interface”, “mature lines”, “mature `ProjStrat`”, “adapters”, and “mature branch weights” with “low individual degree test”, “LDT lines”,