\\\\\u2014 The four generic `consistencyDefect` relabeling and congruence lemmas are buried in the direct-LD transport layer instead of the shared consistency API.  <!-- lane=code -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/Measurements.lean:152` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 Generic functoriality for `Quantum.Measurement.postprocess` is exposed from a QPBT transport module instead of beside the measurement definition.  <!-- lane=code -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F3 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/Measurements.lean:2` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 `TensorSupport` is unused by `Measurements.lean` and reaches its actual consumer, `State.lean`, only transitively.  <!-- lane=code -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F4 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/State.lean:217` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 `directPointNonempty` redundantly shadows the canonical `Pi.instNonempty` instance with a noncomputable global instance.  <!-- lane=code -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F5 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:18` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 The newly linked, completed `ldGame` definition lacks the required statement-level `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok`.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F6 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/Defect.lean:217` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 The public coordinatewise consistency implications lack subordinate blueprint entries stating their premises and restricted scope.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F7 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/Compression.lean:322` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 The two public mixed-defect compression identities lack a blueprint support entry distinguishing them from the still-missing global/global compression.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F8 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree.lean:28` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201ctransports the three mature consistency conclusions to the direct game\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d overstates results that assume the LDT relations and operate on individual polynomial coordinates.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F9 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency.lean:7` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cstable public facade re-exports\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d is software terminology; replace it with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cThis module provides\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F10 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/State.lean:29` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cbridge\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201caliases\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cdownstream consumers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d, and \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cshared API\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d describe implementation structure rather than the mathematical identity.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F11 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/DistanceTheorems/Support.lean:598` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cpure-state bridge\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d and \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cconversion API\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d are banned software language; describe the inverse constructions and quadratic-form identity directly.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F12 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/State.lean:314` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 The new `mature...` public names and repeated \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cmature LDT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d prose encode formalization status rather than mathematical content.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F13 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Pauli.lean:98` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 The two generic normalization identities are formalization-only auxiliaries, but their docstrings do not identify them as such.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F14 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/Compression.lean:40` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cconstructor-preserving\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d and the repeated \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cadapter\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d terminology use Lean/software vocabulary instead of stating the preserved answer forms and correlated-residue extension.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n<!-- findings:end -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Code review\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nF1: `consistencyDefect_uniform_question_equiv`, `consistencyDefect_outcome_equiv`, their combined form, and `consistencyDefect_congr` contain no direct-low-degree data. Keeping them here forces general users to import the complete strategy/state transport stack. Move them beside `consistencyDefect` in `QPBT/Games/Consistency.lean`, or into a lightweight shared consistency-theorems module. This must be fixed before merge.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nF2: `matrixMeasurement_postprocess_comp` is a general theorem about the type defined in `Quantum/Measurement.lean:45`, and its proof also introduces a private replacement for a missing core extensionality theorem. Add an extensionality theorem and namespaced `Measurement.postprocess_comp` beside `Measurement.postprocess`, then reuse it here. At minimum, this theorem should not be exposed from the unrelated `MIPStarRE.QPBT` transport namespace. This must be fixed before merge.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nF3: Removing the import at line 2 still leaves `Measurements.lean` type-correct. The declarations requiring it are `DistanceCalculus.leftPlacedMeasurement`, `rightPlacedMeasurement`, and `placed_product_stateQForm_eq` at `State.lean:61`, `:64`, and `:107`. Move the import to `State.lean` so the dependency is explicit.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nF4: With only the correspondence layer imported, Lean already resolves `Nonempty (Fin D.m \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 DirectScalarQ D)` as `Pi.instNonempty`; after importing `State.lean`, it instead selects `directPointNonempty D`. Remove this overlapping instance. The preceding `directMaturePointNonempty` remains necessary and should be retained.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe source-statement audit found no drift. The three conversion lemmas preserve exactly the two point/global conclusions and the global/global conclusion of `thm:main-formal` in `references/ldt-paper/test_definition.tex:180-202`, including the same `delta`; they introduce no bridge, residual, or proof-obligation input. Their single-coordinate scope is stated explicitly and is consistent with the simultaneous target in `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:413-440`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe `ldGame` change only discharges distribution normalization. Its parameters, registers, distribution, and predicate remain aligned with `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:17-118`, and the added `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.ldGame}` link is appropriate.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe prior proof-integrity and duplication findings are resolved: the custom finite-sum lemma is gone, normalization uses the shared Pauli identity, the pure-state bridge is consolidated in `DistanceTheorems/Support.lean`, `strategyPureState` is reused, the `MainFormal` import is removed, and the specialized consistency wrapper now delegates to the generic conversion. The earlier blueprint-coverage scan remains advisory because no `enforce-blueprint-coverage` label was supplied.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAll changed proof files type-check directly, `git diff --check` passes, and the principal new declarations report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. The two existing `sorry` sites in `LowDegreeGame.lean:184` and `:193` predate this diff and are documented as named Lean proof obligations.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Prose review\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nF1 is a status error, not a signature mismatch. `LdParams` has the blueprint\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2019s positivity, admissibility, and divisibility assumptions, and `ldGame` packages the stated question and answer types, distribution, and predicate. Its former `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u03bc_prob` hole is now closed at `LowDegreeGame.lean:345`, so the definition block should carry statement-level `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFor F2, the source theorem at `ch13_qpbt_test.tex:148` constructs joint polynomial-tuple measurements from a successful strategy. By contrast, the results at `Defect.lean:217` and `:303` fix one coordinate and assume the corresponding `ConsRel`; the result at `:394` assumes a pair of individual polynomial measurements. Record these as explicitly formalization-only support nodes with their full premises. They must not be added to the source-labelled soundness block as evidence for its `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFor F3, `Compression.lean:322` and `:360` prove only the point/global and global/point compression identities. `Measurements.lean:320` explicitly records that separate diagonal-block averaging does not provide global/global compression. A subordinate blueprint node should state exactly these two valid identities and preserve that limitation.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nF4 should say, for example: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201c`Transport.Consistency` reexpresses the three single-polynomial LDT consistency relations in direct coordinates, with the first two taken at a fixed tuple coordinate.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d This avoids implying that `exists_direct_ld_soundness`, whose construction of joint tuple measurements remains open, has been established.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFor F6, replace the comment by a mathematical sentence such as: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cThe following exported identities identify pure-state expectation with the Euclidean quadratic form used in the consistency calculations.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d For F7, say that the construction sends a pure state to its Euclidean coordinate vector and that the displayed theorem identifies its quadratic form with density-state evaluation.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFor F8, use `LDT` or `seed-indexed LDT` in prose and prefixes such as `ldt...` or `seedIndexed...` in the new public names. \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cMature\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d distinguishes implementation history, not two mathematical notions. For F9, begin with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cThis formalization-only normalization identity supports...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d and retain the cited EPR and seed-fiber constructions. For F10, use \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cthe answer equivalence preserves point answers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d and \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cthe correlated-residue extension of the strategy\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNo changed `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\notready` tag is stale. The existing source soundness entry correctly has statement-level `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok` without proof-level `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok`; the new conversion results do not change that status.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nPrior-ledger triage: the cited sum helper, unused import, duplicate state conversion, and duplicate scale calculation are absent from this head. The remaining generic-conversion concern belongs to the code-review lane. The prior blueprint-coverage warning remains relevant and is narrowed here to F2 and F3.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSummary: 3 blueprint/status issues and 7 prose issues. No existing blueprint-to-Lean quantifier or conclusion mismatch was found, but the missing support nodes must not be repaired by overstating the source soundness theorem.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"state\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"COMMENTED\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"html_url\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pu