k a proof-level `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok`.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F7 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:2014` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 The two completed compression identities lack a proof-level `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok`.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F8 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree.lean:23` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cmature\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cinterface\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d, and \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cadapters\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d describe implementation status rather than mathematics.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F9 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/State.lean:30` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cexported identities\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d is Lean-specific implementation language.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ ] F10 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Transport/Consistency/State.lean:134` \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2014 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201cLDT state interface\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u201d is software terminology rather than mathematical prose.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n<!-- findings:end -->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Code review\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nF1 is a genuine statement-scope mismatch. `def:ld-meas` at `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:128-132` explicitly defines these measurements as POVMs, matching `lem:ld-soundness` in `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:413-438`, which produces measurements \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\(G^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm A},G^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm B}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\). The linked Lean declarations instead require `ProjMeas` at `Defect.lean:110`, `:196`, and `:286-287`. Projectivity is not a Lean boundary condition; it restricts the mathematical domain and prevents applying these declarations directly