 that the claimed form follows from neither, the corrected\\n  1161\\t\\tdeficit assertion in the proof of Lemma~\\\\ref{lem:claim-17-2}, and the\\n  1162\\t\\tcandidate repairs with their open obligations --- is given in\\n  1163\\t\\t\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}.\\n  1164\\t\\\\end{remark}\\n  1165\\t\\n  1166\\tThe measurements of Lemma~\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-12} and Lemma~\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}\\n  1167\\tconstitute a strategy for the classical low individual degree game in $2m+2$\\n  1168\\tvariables. Applying the quantum soundness of that game yields a single\\n  1169\\tprojective measurement whose outcomes are pairs of global polynomials.\\n  1170\\t\\n  1171\\t\\\\begin{lemma}[The global polynomial-pair measurement]\\n  1172\\t\\t\\\\label{lem:qld-4-7}\\n  1173\\t\\t\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.Poly, MIPStarRE.QPBT.PolyPair, MIPStarRE.QPBT.evalAt}\\n  1174\\t\\t\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.GlobalPairWitness}\\n  1175\\t\\t\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_globalPairWitness}\\n  1176\\t\\t\\\\notready\\n  1177\\t\\t\\\\uses{def:polyfunc, def:expanded-state, def:expanded-point-measurement,\\n  1178\\t\\t\\tdef:consistency, def:bracket, def:ideg-deg-polynomials}\\n  1179\\t\\t% Statement as in the source (references/qpbt-paper/\\n  1180\\t\\t% 14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex, lem:qld-4-7). The proof\\n  1181\\t\\t% instantiates the classical low individual degree game, and Theorem\\n  1182\\t\\t% lem:ld-soundness, at dimension 2m+2, which def:ld-game admits only\\n  1183\\t\\t% when the dimension divides q; the source performs the instantiation\\n  1184\\t\\t% without securing this condition. See rem:qld-4-7-divisibility.\\n  1185\\t\\tThere exists a function\\n  1186\\t\\t$\\\\delta_S(\\\\eps,m,d,q) = a(md)^a(\\\\eps^b + q^{-b} + 2^{-bmd})$, for some\\n  1187\\t\\tuniversal constants $a > 1$ and $0 < b < 1$, such that the following\\n  1188\\t\\tholds. For\\n  1189\\t\\t$\\\\hilb \\\\in \\\\{\\\\hilb_{\\\\mathsf{A}}, \\\\hilb_{\\\\mathsf{B}}\\\\}$ there\\n  1190\\t\\texists a projective measurement $\\\\{\\\\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z}\\\\}$ acting on\\n  1191\\t\\t$\\\\hilb \\\\ot (\\\\C^q)^{\\\\ot M}$, with outcomes consisting of pairs\\n  1192\\t\\t$(g_X, g_Z)$ of polynomials, each in $\\\\mathrm{ideg}_{d,m}(\\\\F_q)$, such\\n  1193\\t\\tthat for $W \\\\in \\\\{X, Z\\\\}$, on average over uniformly random\\n  1194\\t\\t$u \\\\in \\\\F_q^m$,\\n  1195\\t\\t\\\\begin{align}\\n  1196\\t\\t\\t\\\\big(\\\\hat{S}_{[\\\\mathrm{eval}_u(\\\\cdot_W) = a]}\\n  1197\\t\\t\\t\\\\big)_{\\\\mathsf{A}\\\\mathsf{A}'}\\n  1198\\t\\t\\t&\\\\simeq_{\\\\delta_S}\\n  1199\\t\\t\\t\\\\big(\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\mathrm{Point},W),u}_{a}\\n  1200\\t\\t\\t\\\\big)_{\\\\mathsf{B}\\\\mathsf{A}''}\\\\,,\\n  1201\\t\\t\\t\\\\label{eq:qld-s-point-con-alice} \\\\\\\\\\n  1202\\t\\t\\t\\\\big(\\\\hat{S}_{[\\\\mathrm{eval}_u(\\\\cdot_W) = a]}\\n  1203\\t\\t\\t\\\\big)_{\\\\mathsf{B}\\\\mathsf{B}'}\\n  1204\\t\\t\\t&\\\\simeq_{\\\\delta_S}\\n  1205\\t\\t\\t\\\\big(\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\mathrm{Point},W),u}_{a}\\n  1206\\t\\t\\t\\\\big)_{\\\\mathsf{A}\\\\mathsf{B}''}\\\\,,\\n  1207\\t\\t\\t\\\\label{eq:qld-s-point-con-bob}\\n  1208\\t\\t\\\\end{align}\\n  1209\\t\\twhere $\\\\mathrm{eval}_u(\\\\cdot_W)$ denotes the evaluation at the point $u$\\n  1210\\t\\tof the first outcome $g_X$ if $W = X$, and of the second outcome $g_Z$\\n  1211\\t\\tif $W = Z$.\\n  1212\\t\\\\end{lemma}\\n  1213\\t\\\\begin{proof}\\n  1214\\t\\t\\\\uses{lem:qld-4-13, lem:qld-4-12, thm:naimark, lem:ld-soundness,\\n  1215\\t\\t\\tdef:ld-game, fact:agreement, fact:add-a-proj2,\\n   100\\t      ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧\\n   101\\t        ∃ deltaCombine : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr₂ deltaCombine ∧\\n   102\\t          ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε : ℝ) (S : ProjectiveSetting P ε),\\n   103\\t            ∃ points : CombinedPointsWitness S (deltaQ ε),\\n   104\\t              Nonempty (ExtendedLinesWitness S points\\n   105\\t                (C * (P.m : ℝ) *\\n   106\\t                  deltaCombine ε ((P.m * P.d : ℕ) / (